<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=spinning-wheel">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spinning wheel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The spinning wheel is a device in which a hand- or foot-turned wheel drives the spindle that spins fibres into thread or yarn; its origin is disputed, and some scholars hold that Chinese dictionaries of the 2nd century CE mention it. Others place its invention in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> or the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>, where evidence points to it being known by 1030; the earliest clear illustration was drawn in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 1237. It spread from the Middle East to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> by the 13th century and raised the productivity of thread-making more than tenfold.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spinning-wheel.jpg" alt="Spinning wheel" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An_amorous_encounter_-_Smithfield_Decretals_(Decretals_of_Gregory_IX)_(c.1340),_f.139_-_BL_Royal_MS_10_E_IV.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Hunting for the deerskin trade gave way to farming and herding, with maize, cotton, cattle, hogs and orchards, while <b>spinning wheels</b> and looms supplied by United States agents made cloth at home.</blockquote><a href="/empire/cherokee-nation">Cherokee Nation · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>New machines came in from the Islamic world, such as geared water-wheels, and the earliest clear reference to a <b>spinning wheel</b> in India dates from 1350.</blockquote><a href="/societies/delhi-sultanate">Social Hierarchy of the Delhi Sultanate</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>2nd century CE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>China</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Its origin is disputed: Kuhn and Cheng argue for China, where dictionaries of the 2nd century CE mention it; others place it in India, or in the Middle East, where it was known by 1030.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/spinning-jenny">Spinning jenny<span>c. 1764</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=spinning-wheel">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
